# ==== T-FMT-C · `catch (e):` arm body — no `do:` insertion, no blank
#
# AXIS (2 cells): inline recovery · block recovery.
#
# The parser wraps a `catch`/`rethrow` INDENTED body as a SYNTHETIC
# `Expr::Do` (`parse_body_or_expr`), the same AST variant an author gets by
# writing `do:` explicitly. Re-emitting `do:` for the synthetic one is a
# formatter-invented keyword; deleting it for the author-written one destroys
# what the author spelled. `Expr::Do.author_spelled` is what tells them apart.
#
# RED pre-fix (recorded 2026-08-11):
#   * block cell — a spurious BLANK line after the enclosing var-decl.
#   * `tests/fixtures/known_gaps/catch_binding_throw_in_match_arm_ice.gg`
#     was mutated by `gg fmt` into `catch (e): do:` + a blank (2 hunks), i.e.
#     the formatter rewrote an ICE reproducer's shape. That fixture is the
#     in-tree cell for the `do:`-INSERTION direction; this file holds the
#     no-insertion + no-blank pins for the ordinary shapes.

int risky(int x):
    throw "boom"

void inline_recovery(int x):
    int v = risky(x) catch (e): -1
    print(v)

void block_recovery(int x):
    int v = risky(x) catch (e):
        int t = x + 1
        t * 2
    print(v)

void main():
    inline_recovery(1)
    block_recovery(1)
